cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Deterministic State Reduction via Golden-Ratio Polynomials for Low-Latency Quantum Boundary Commitments"
authors:
  - family-names: Sanders
    given-names: Jacarri
    affiliation: "Even The Odds Foundry LLC / Kerna-Ledger Engineering Group"
    email: eventheoddsfoundry@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/jabrahns-source/phi-boundary-commitments"
url: "https://github.com/jabrahns-source/phi-boundary-commitments"
abstract: >-
  Classical-to-quantum interface architectures suffer from computational overhead and non-deterministic timing drift when translating continuous quantum phase dynamics into classical registers. This work presents a deterministic algebraic engine that bypasses FPUs by exploiting the minimal polynomial of the golden ratio. Any Fibonacci-weighted state sequence reduces to a two-dimensional integer state (A, B) over native u64 registers. A randomized commitment with 256-bit blinding salt is proven computationally binding and information-theoretically hiding under the Random Oracle Model. Gate-level correctness is formally verified with Z3 bit-vector SMT.
keywords:
  - Quantum Cryptography
  - Golden Ratio
  - Formal Verification
  - SMT Solvers
  - ALU Bypass
  - Computational Hiding
  - Hybrid Games
  - Integer Pipeline
  - Deterministic Compute
